# Plan 6 Task 17b — the bisect markers, as a patch against the Java clone's read-only sources.
#
# WHAT THIS IS
#   The `router-dac2020-bm01` `ripupPassNo >= 2` divergence (quirk #74) was bisected in six
#   levels. Level 1 needs no patching: `scripts/differential/java/P6T17bProbe.java` decorates
#   `board.communication.idGenerator` and labels every allocation by a `StackWalker` frame.
#   Levels 2-6 need markers *inside* freerouting, and this patch is them. It is the artefact that
#   makes the task's load-bearing measurement — 2358 `PolylineTrace.change` calls, of which 1403
#   disagree between Java's reference comparison and a value one — re-runnable.
#
# THE JAVA TREE STAYS READ-ONLY.
#   Apply into a scratch copy and put the compiled classes *in front of* the jar; never into the
#   clone.
#
#     JDIR=../freerouting/src/main/java          # the clone, untouched
#     JAR=../freerouting/build/libs/freerouting-current-executable.jar
#     J25=/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@25/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home
#     SCRATCH=$(mktemp -d)
#     ( cd "$JDIR" && git ls-files \
#         app/freerouting/autoroute/maze/MazeSearchEngine.java \
#         app/freerouting/autoroute/maze/AutorouteEngine.java \
#         app/freerouting/board/searchtree/ShapeSearchTree45Degree.java \
#         app/freerouting/board/searchtree/SearchTreeManager.java \
#         app/freerouting/board/trace/PolylineTrace.java \
#         app/freerouting/datastructures/MinAreaTree.java \
#       | cpio -pdm "$SCRATCH" )
#     ( cd "$SCRATCH" && patch -p1 < <abs path>/scripts/differential/java/p6t17b-bisect.patch )
#     "$J25/bin/javac" -nowarn -cp "$JAR" -d "$SCRATCH/classes" $(find "$SCRATCH" -name '*.java')
#
# VALIDATE BEFORE TRUSTING ANY MARKER — this is not optional.
#   Compile the *unpatched* copies the same way and run `P6T1` with them ahead of the jar; the
#   output must be byte-identical to the plain-jar run, which is what proves the clone's sources
#   and the jar are the same code. With the patch applied and the markers switched off (the
#   default), the same comparison must still hold; it did, on 20 connections of
#   `Issue508-DAC2020_bm01` at `ripupPassNo = 2`.
#
# RUN
#   The markers are gated on two `public static` fields the patch adds to `MazeSearchEngine`, and
#   `P6T17bProbe` sets them from the environment:
#
#     P6T17B_DEEP=1  — OCCUPY / OTHERLAYERS / ROOMDOORS / PUSH / DOORSEC (the maze queue),
#                      CROOM_IN / CROOM_CAND / ROOM (room completion),
#                      NODE / LEAF / LEAFROOM / RESTRAIN (the 45-degree completeShape walk),
#                      TINS / TREM (+ a stack signature) and SMINS / SMREM (tree mutations),
#                      CHANGE (PolylineTrace.change's two index pairs, identity *and* value)
#                      — all for the one connection `P6T17bProbe`'s `k` names.
#     P6T17B_DEEP=all — the same markers for *every* connection. Use it on a handful of
#                      connections only: over a whole board its stderr runs to gigabytes.
#     P6T17B_CHANGE=1 — CHANGE alone, for every connection. This is the task's **pinning
#                      measurement**, and it is cheap enough to run over a whole board:
#
#                        P6T17B_CHANGE=1 "$J25/bin/java" ... P6T17bProbe \
#                            ../freerouting/fixtures/Issue508-DAC2020_bm01.dsn 267 2 2>c.txt
#                        grep -c '^CHANGE' c.txt                                  # 2358
#                        grep '^CHANGE' c.txt | awk '{split($4,a,"="); split($6,b,"=");
#                          split($5,c,"="); split($7,d,"=");
#                          if (a[2] != b[2] || c[2] != d[2]) n++} END {print n}'  # 1403
#
#                      `idFirst`/`idLast` are Java's reference comparison, `vFirst`/`vLast` the
#                      same two indices computed with `Line.equals`. The port agrees with the
#                      first pair on all 2358 and would disagree on 1403 with the second.
#     P6T17B_TREE=1  — TREENODE: a pre-order dump of the whole autoroute tree (leaf/inner flag
#                      plus each node's bounding octagon) once per connection, at its first
#                      `completeShape`. This is the level that put the first structural
#                      divergence at connection 92, node 414 of 5063.
#
#     P6T17B_DEEP=1 "$J25/bin/java" -Djava.awt.headless=true -Duser.language=en -Duser.country=US \
#         -XX:+UnlockExperimentalVMOptions -XX:hashCode=2 \
#         -cp <probe-classes>:"$SCRATCH/classes":"$JAR" \
#         app.freerouting.autoroute.maze.P6T17bProbe \
#         ../freerouting/fixtures/Issue508-DAC2020_bm01.dsn 267 2 2>markers.txt
#
#   Every marker goes to **stderr**, so the driver's own stdout stays diffable. The port side was
#   instrumented to match with env-gated `eprintln!`s at the mirrored statements; none of that is
#   committed (it would be production-path tracing), and the report's §3 names each pair.
#
